{%- comment -%}
  PG Page Logo: make the wordmark on the page templates (Track Your Order,
  Contact, policies) match the one on the homepage and PDP.

  Two things are wrong there. The mark renders purple and blurry instead of the
  near-white #F6DBFF with a tight glow, and a solid black bar sits directly
  under it.

  The black bar is almost certainly the retired logo art. pe-logo swaps every
  header <img> to the vector badge and sets mix-blend-mode:normal -- correct for
  a transparent SVG, but the old raster asset had a black box baked in, and
  pg-dark was relying on mix-blend-mode:screen to knock that black out. Any
  header image on these templates that pg-mobile's display:none list misses
  therefore paints its black box. These templates use the wordmark as the brand
  mark, so the images are hidden outright here.

  The colour is restated with -webkit-text-fill-color as well as color, because
  a gradient text-fill anywhere up the chain would otherwise win, and the glow
  is set to pe-logo's tighter three-stop shadow rather than the wide 12px/.9
  alpha one, which is what reads as blur.

  Scoped to body.template-page* so the homepage, PDP and cart are untouched.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
/* the wordmark: same white and same glow as everywhere else */
html body[class*="template-page"] a.pg-wordmark.pg-wordmark,
html body[class*="template-page"] .pgc-logo a.pg-wordmark.pg-wordmark{
  color:#F6DBFF !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color:#F6DBFF !important;
  background:none !important;
  background-image:none !important;
  text-shadow:0 0 6px rgba(246,219,255,.5),0 0 17px rgba(199,155,234,.38),0 0 40px rgba(139,68,190,.26) !important;
  filter:none !important;
}

/* the black bar: retired logo art with its black box no longer knocked out */
html body[class*="template-page"] .pgc-logo img,
html body[class*="template-page"] .pgc-head img,
html body[class*="template-page"] .pgf-head img,
html body[class*="template-page"] .pgh-logo img,
html body[class*="template-page"] .pgx-logo img{
  display:none !important;
}
</style>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Page Logo", "settings": []}
{% endschema %}
